{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1292991-quintessence-and-avatar-rating","id":1292991,"title":"Quintessence and Avatar Rating.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-01T05:22:59-08:00","id":1292991,"title":"Quintessence and Avatar Rating.","content":"Let's say my avatar rating is 1, and I'm trying to cast something which involves a rank 5 sphere, and it's vulgar. So the default difficulty would be 9. Ideally best way to get the -3 diff modifier would naturally be spending QPs, however, due to the avatar rating being 1 I'm restricted to spending only 1 QP per turn. Is there a way to somehow surpass this limitation? I remember there being a way of spending more QPs than your avatar rating per turn if you've prime 3, however I'm unable to find this in the book eh.<br /> <br /> Would really appreciate some help here, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:09:53-08:00","id":1292998,"title":"","content":"The Avatar Rating *is* the hard limit for channeling Quintessence into effects. However, using Prime1+ you can draw more than your Avatar Rating out of a node (or rather, store more than your Avatar Rating, period), and Prime 3 allows channeling Quintessence into and from Object, etc.<br /> But no, neither Revised nor M20 seem to indicate that actual Effect Channeling can be pushed through the limit of the Avatar Rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-01-2019, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:48:49-08:00","id":1293010,"title":"","content":"There's a rule in HDYDT that seems to allow such feats:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT p.43</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Amount of Quintessence Used</u><br /> <b>Game-wise, a mage must have at least three dots in either the Prime or Primal Utility Spheres if she wants to use \u201cmore than her share\u201d of energy. </b>Any mage with an Avatar Background can absorb that Background\u2019s worth of Quintessence from a Node or Tass, or use the points of Quintessence in the Quintessence wheel on her character sheet. In order to use more points of Quintessence than she has in her Avatar Background rating, however, and in order to use Quintessence from other sources, she must have at least Rank 3 in the Prime<br /> or Primal Utility Spheres.<b> As an example, Jinx (Avatar 5) can use up to five points of Quintessence per turn, while Sabra, (Avatar 1) may use only one point of Quintessence per turn until he achieves Prime 3. As the Base Damage and Duration chart explains, the amount of Quintessence a mage with Prime 3 or higher mage can employ within a single Effect is based upon the number of successes rolled. If Penny Dreadful\u2019s player, for example, rolls three successes, then Penny can employ up to six points of Quintessence with that Effect</b>; if she rolls five, then Penny can use up to 10 points that Effect. This, of course, assumes that Penny Dreadful has Prime 3 or higher; considering that Penny\u2019s been around for a while, though, that\u2019s a pretty safe assumption.<b> If Penny doesn\u2019t have Prime 3, though, then Penny is stuck using her Avatar rating\u2019s worth of Quintessence, period.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I was aware that it was possible to <i>move arround </i>more than your Avatar share of Quintessence with Prime, but that it's possible to actually <i>use </i>(to any purpose) more than the Avatar rating per turn it's a bit of a surprise. Still the wording of the entry certainly implies that it is possible.<br /> <br /> Note that this it's an Effect, it has to be rolled, it's an active use of magick and not a passive benefit of having Prime 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:11:25-08:00","id":1293017,"title":"","content":"I find it kind of amusing that that ruling is in none of the core books. One'd figure that it'd be put in the same section where the rules say 'A Mage can only channel up to their Avatar Rating in Quintessence into an effect'. C'est la vie.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that this it's an Effect, it has to be rolled, it's an active use of magick and not a passive benefit of having Prime 3. </div> </div> </div>That's also a bit misleading there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It is a passive function of Prime 3, but it is based on the amount of successes rolled for the effect you want to dump extra Quintessence into <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (i.e. you don't need two Arete rolls)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T15:55:08-08:00","id":1293174,"title":"","content":"If that's the case then it shouldn't be usable for what the OP wants. I mean, you just can't reduce the difficulty of a roll<i> retroactively. </i>Imagine that (i.e: you would reduce the difficulty retroactively, then you would be able to expend more Quintessence, then reduce the difficluty a bit more...). That would be crazy.<br /> <br /> Probably the intention was for that power to be limited to &quot;Other uses of Qintessence&quot;, as it can be assumed by how it's written in M20 (still very misleading as it's a small line under a table with 0 clarification about how it relates to the system in general)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-01-2019, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T04:35:33-08:00","id":1293446,"title":"","content":"I think so, too.It's a confusing bit, and up to interpretation.<br /> <br /> Either:<br /> 1) You have to roll twice, and the first roll is for Prime 3 raises the limit of Quintessence you can spend on...the next turn and effect I presume?<br /> or<br /> 2) You roll once, and it's for transferring quintessence from one thing into the other, and/or using Quintessence in other ways than lowering effect difficulty.<br /> <br /> Lemme check the HDYDT page real quick.<br /> <br /> [Reading Intensifies]<br /> <br /> Hmmh. Yeah, okay. It's still unclear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It could be interpreted both ways, but what stands out is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As the Base Damage and Duration chart explains, the<br /> amount of Quintessence a mage with Prime 3 or higher mage<br /> can employ <b>within a single Effect</b> is based upon the number<br /> of successes rolled. If Penny Dreadful\u2019s player, for example,<br /> <b>rolls three successes</b>, then Penny can employ up to six points<br /> of Quintessence <b>with that Effect</b> </div> </div> </div>Personally I pretty much read it as Option 2. Option 1 would also make the Avatar Background even more obsolete for Prime Mages. Its major spiel *is* the fact that it determines how much Quintessence you can use for making effects easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-03-2019, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T16:52:28-08:00","id":1294223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1292991-quintessence-and-avatar-rating?p=1293446#post1293446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think so, too.It's a confusing bit, and up to interpretation.<br /> <br /> Either:<br /> 1) You have to roll twice, and the first roll is for Prime 3 raises the limit of Quintessence you can spend on...the next turn and effect I presume?<br /> or<br /> 2) You roll once, and it's for transferring quintessence from one thing into the other, and/or using Quintessence in other ways than lowering effect difficulty.<br /> <br /> Lemme check the HDYDT page real quick.<br /> <br /> [Reading Intensifies]<br /> <br /> Hmmh. Yeah, okay. It's still unclear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It could be interpreted both ways, but what stands out is:<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I pretty much read it as Option 2. Option 1 would also make the Avatar Background even more obsolete for Prime Mages. Its major spiel *is* the fact that it determines how much Quintessence you can use for making effects easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you're getting at, but I'm pretty sure that it's #1. If you have Prime 3 or higher you can spend a turn doing an effect that allows you to temporarily spend extra Quintessence. This makes sense within Mage since Spheres tend to be active rather than reflexive or passive.<br /> <br /> Having Avatar 1 is still a significant disadvantage here; you have to roll a Prime 3 effect, which means a Difficulty 6 roll. That means risk of Paradox (although it's Coincidental). You then have to roll the other effect, spending whatever Quintessence you're allowed to. By contrast the Avatar 5 Mage can simply do all of this effortlessly.<br /> <br /> But a neat upside is that Avatar 1 isn't horribly limiting if you're tinkering in the lab. You don't need to have high Avatar to create Wonders, for example, if you can use Prime to turn yourself into a temporary nexus of energy. It's all very cool and neat for slow and steady work. Avatar will always give that cool bonus when you're working with no preparation.<br /> <br /> And Avatar has the oft-forgotten benefit of soaking &quot;spiritual&quot; attacks by Spirits, such as fire blasts and electrical discharges. And in some Chronicles that can be game-changing; 5 dots of soak against Lethal or Aggravated damage for 5 freebies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-05-2019, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}